cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QForge in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "QForge: An Event-Driven Quantum Circuit Simulator in Java"
abstract: >-
  QForge is an exact quantum circuit simulator written in Java 17. It executes
  time-ordered quantum events against a state-vector backend (up to 30 qubits) or a
  density-matrix backend (up to 12 qubits), applies depolarizing, dephasing, and
  amplitude-damping noise through Kraus operators, measures arbitrary Hermitian
  observables with projective state collapse, and includes reference circuits for
  Grover search, the quantum Fourier transform, phase estimation, VQE, QAOA,
  Trotterized evolution, the Shor code, quantum walks, a quantum neural network, and
  a swap-test kernel classifier.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mechalikh
    given-names: Charafeddine
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-25
repository-code: "https://github.com/CharafeddineMechalikh/QForge"
